  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand why that looks low. Under our policy, a card refund on a promo order has to account for the discount, and you didn't pay the full $15 for that pho. $3.00 of the promo discount applied to it. So the card refund is $12.00, and the $3.00 comes back to you as account credit. That means you get the full $15.00 in total value. I can't refund the full $15 to the card.\n\nI'll go ahead with the $12.00 card refund and the $3.00 credit now.\n\nI've done both, Owen:\n\n- **$12.00 refund** to your Visa ending 4242. It should arrive in 3-5 business days.\n- **$3.00 account credit**, which is already in your balance for your next order.\n\nAgain, I'm sorry about the missing pho. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I get it now. So I'm getting $12 back on the card and $3 as credit, which covers the full $15 in total. That works for me, thanks for sorting it out."
